### EventHub API — example requests
### Use with VS Code "REST Client" or "Thunder Client" extension.
### Run requests top to bottom; copy tokens/ids from responses into the
### variables below as you go.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:4000
@accessToken =eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9.eyJzdWIiOiI2YTRkZDdhM2IwNGM3MjcyNDY3ZDZkZWQiLCJyb2xlIjoibWVtYmVyIiwiaWF0IjoxNzgzNDg2ODgwLCJleHAiOjE3ODM0ODc3ODB9.Ggjf0qPO4c1TVkbouLHvJEuV3220xPWFoSQvtICAFs8
@refreshToken =8448fc3747c619162e42cb0aa6f65000940cc9046c0df9d8f6f10326a1bf6e47a83566187db68ba678c67fe67645d8ee
@eventId =6a4dd77eb04c7272467d6dec
@reviewId = PASTE_REVIEW_ID_HERE


### ============================================================
### AUTH
### ============================================================

### Register an organizer
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Alice Organizer",
  "email": "alice@example.com",
  "password": "supersecret1",
  "role": "organizer"
}


### Register a member
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Bob Member",
  "email": "bob@example.com",
  "password": "supersecret1",
  "role": "member"
}


### Login (copy accessToken/refreshToken from the response above into the variables)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "bob@example.com",
  "password": "supersecret1"
}


### Get own profile (requires accessToken)
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/profile
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}


### Refresh tokens (rotates refreshToken — copy the NEW one from the response)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "refreshToken": "{{refreshToken}}"
}


### Logout (revokes refreshToken server-side)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/logout
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "refreshToken": "{{refreshToken}}"
}


### ============================================================
### EVENTS
### ============================================================

### List events (public, no auth) — filters + pagination
GET {{baseUrl}}/events?category=tech&page=1&limit=10


### List events by date range
GET {{baseUrl}}/events?dateFrom=2026-08-01&dateTo=2026-12-31


### Create event (organizer only — use an organizer's accessToken)
POST {{baseUrl}}/events
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Backend Meetup",
  "description": "A meetup about REST APIs, MongoDB, and JWT auth flows.",
  "category": "tech",
  "location": "Yerevan, Armenia",
  "startTime": "2026-09-01T18:00:00.000Z",
  "endTime": "2026-09-01T21:00:00.000Z",
  "capacity": 2
}


### Get event by id (public)
GET {{baseUrl}}/events/{{eventId}}


### Update event (organizer, must be the owner)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/events/{{eventId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "capacity": 5,
  "location": "Yerevan, Armenia — new venue"
}


### Add an agenda item (organizer, must be the owner)
POST {{baseUrl}}/events/{{eventId}}/agenda
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Intro to JWT rotation",
  "startTime": "2026-09-01T18:00:00.000Z",
  "endTime": "2026-09-01T18:30:00.000Z",
  "speaker": "Alice Organizer"
}


### Delete event (organizer, must be the owner)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/events/{{eventId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}


### ============================================================
### ATTENDANCE — use a MEMBER's accessToken here
### ============================================================

### Join an event
POST {{baseUrl}}/events/{{eventId}}/join
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}


### Join again with the same user -> expect 409 ALREADY_JOINED
POST {{baseUrl}}/events/{{eventId}}/join
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}


### Leave an event
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/events/{{eventId}}/join
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}


### List attendees (public)
GET {{baseUrl}}/events/{{eventId}}/attendees?page=1&limit=20


### ============================================================
### REVIEWS
### ============================================================

### Create a review — only works if the user attended AND the event has ended.
### To test the happy path, create an event with startTime/endTime in the past
### (organizers can't normally do this via the create-event validation ordering
### assumptions, so seed one directly via mongosh if needed for this test).
POST {{baseUrl}}/events/{{eventId}}/reviews
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "rating": 5,
  "comment": "Great talks, well organized."
}


### Try reviewing the same event again -> expect 409 REVIEW_ALREADY_EXISTS
POST {{baseUrl}}/events/{{eventId}}/reviews
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "rating": 4,
  "comment": "Trying to review twice."
}


### List reviews for an event (public) — includes average rating summary
GET {{baseUrl}}/events/{{eventId}}/reviews?page=1&limit=10


### Delete a review (only the review's own author)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/reviews/{{reviewId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}


### ============================================================
### ERROR CASES WORTH DEMONSTRATING
### ============================================================

### Missing access token -> 401 TOKEN_MISSING
POST {{baseUrl}}/events
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Should fail",
  "description": "No token provided.",
  "category": "tech",
  "location": "Nowhere",
  "startTime": "2026-09-01T18:00:00.000Z",
  "endTime": "2026-09-01T21:00:00.000Z",
  "capacity": 10
}


### Member trying to create an event -> 403 ROLE_NOT_ALLOWED
### (use a member's accessToken here)
POST {{baseUrl}}/events
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Should fail",
  "description": "Members cannot create events.",
  "category": "tech",
  "location": "Nowhere",
  "startTime": "2026-09-01T18:00:00.000Z",
  "endTime": "2026-09-01T21:00:00.000Z",
  "capacity": 10
}


### Invalid body (endTime before startTime) -> 400 VALIDATION_ERROR
POST {{baseUrl}}/events
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Bad time range",
  "description": "endTime is before startTime.",
  "category": "tech",
  "location": "Nowhere",
  "startTime": "2026-09-01T21:00:00.000Z",
  "endTime": "2026-09-01T18:00:00.000Z",
  "capacity": 10
}
